{"name":"Tickled Pink","hex":"#efa7bf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tickled pink","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very pleased; delighted; thrilled."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of tickle pink"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tickled_pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tickled Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Tickled Pink was an hour-long American television special which aired multiple times during July, 2006, chronicled television shows that homosexuals have identified with over the years. The show featured such entertainers as Richard Andreoli, Kelsey Grammer, Sandra Bernhard, Diahann Carroll, Susan Saint James, Bruce Vilanch, Marc Cherry, Lynda Carter, Bob Mackie, Jean Smart, Jason Stuart, Frank DeCaro, Barbara Eden, Mike Gray, Carson Kressley, Rue McClanahan, Judy Gold, Thom Filicia, and Mario Cantone. Tickled Pink was produced for TV Land by Linda Ellerbee’s Lucky Duck Productions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tickled_Pink","wikidata":"Q7800706"},{"title":"Tickled Pink (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Tickled Pink was an anthology series of self contained short comedies screened by the ABC, airing for two seasons in 1978 and 1981."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tickled_Pink_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q140611194"},{"title":"Tickled","blocks":[{"text":"Tickled is a 2016 New Zealand documentary about \"competitive endurance tickling\" and videos featuring it, and the practices of those producing the videos. It is directed by David Farrier and Dylan Reeve."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Tickled.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tickled","wikidata":"Q24042656"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white 